      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c8f538975056470640f1d9f|full_name}: this is wrong.\n\nFirst of all, you shouldn't have to mangle your avatar to get it working in FBT. You're implying that the default Nikei and Y-Bot are not made for full body, in which case it seems like a very hard bar to clear.\n\nThe viewpoint detachment is simply due to how the IK is set up, with Full Body Biped IK and a Head Effector. The viewpoint doesn't 100% dictate where the head bone goes, so if you get further away from the idle pose it'll detach more.\n\nOn top of that, the generally accepted \"fullbody fix\" still doesn't fix most of these issues. Even one of the devs (hackspanner) commented that this fix should be avoided if possible, since the IK wasn't made that way. And to be honest, the fix *is* a bit of a hackjob, forcing the spine length to be zero like that.\n\nEven a \"fixed\" avatar will only see the issues *mitigated*, not fixed entirely.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5cb810f27c99a94e89d3d0b2",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5ad4ba851ab6da0782c502ca",
