      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "What I think they should do is a two armature system to avoid the proportions bit and the recalibrating bit. With having a control armature that matches your real world proportions and then the armature of your actual avatar copying that over. That way you can just calibrate once at the start and then easily switch between any of your other avatars without having to calibrate again until your next playthrough.\n\nI'm not 100% sure how well storing the calibration would be though since it could be easy for there to be shifts on how you're holding the control or where exactly your trackers are placed between play sessions.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
